IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-core`
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 5/12/2025" -- LAYER 1, PART 9, SECTIONS 76 TO 80
-- (maternity: the length of the absence, the benefit period, the pay, when it is paid,
-- the notice a female employee gives).  Part ea2 of the encoding; the keel's `ea-core`
-- declares the nouns, `ea-definitions` the Act's own definitions.
--
-- Source text: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes
-- Online (inputs/EmA1968.txt).  It is not the official text.  The line numbers in the
-- `-- src:` lines are lines of that file.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its own words.
-- NOTHING means the Act does not answer on these facts (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and
-- NOTHING (ea2)").  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- INPUTS THAT ARE ANOTHER SECTION'S ANSWER (PLAN s 4 seams, taken as MAYBE inputs):
--   `the person is a female employee`  MAYBE BOOLEAN: the keel's `s 2(1) "employee" the person
--        is one` joined with the fact that the employee is female (see the first rule).
--   `the answer of sch 3 gross rate of pay per day`  MAYBE NUMBER: seam S6, the Third Schedule
--        (part ea3).  Never recomputed here.
--   `the answer of sch 5 days`  MAYBE NUMBER: seam S8, the Fifth Schedule (part ea3).
--
-- DAYS AND WEEKS.  The Act's "week" is a period of 7 consecutive days (s 2(1) "week"), so 4, 8
-- and 12 weeks are 28, 56 and 84 days.  Where the day of the confinement falls (fork F1 in
-- NOTES.md): the 4 weeks "immediately before" end on the day before it; the 8 weeks
-- "immediately after" begin on the day itself, so the 12 weeks are 84 days in a row.

§ `Part 9 -- who is a female employee, and the length of the absence (s 76(1))`

-- "female employee" is not defined by the Act.  It is an employee (the keel's definition,
-- passed in as that definition's answer) who is female.
-- src:2765 | 76.—(1) Subject to this section, every female employee is entitled
-- src:2766 | to absent herself from work —
@ref s 76(1) "every female employee" (src:2765-2766)
GIVEN `the answer of s 2(1) "employee"` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is female` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(1) the person is a female employee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of s 2(1) "employee"`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST `the person is female`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every female employee"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is an employee is the answer of s 2(1) "employee", which the Act did not give on these facts
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 76(1): "Subject to this section, every female employee is entitled to absent herself from work".
-- The entitlement is given to female employees only; for anyone else the section is silent.
-- src:2765 | 76.—(1) Subject to this section, every female employee is entitled
-- src:2766 | to absent herself from work —
@ref s 76(1) (src:2765-2766)
GIVEN `the person is a female employee` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(1) the female employee is entitled to absent herself from work` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person is a female employee`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is to "every female employee" and the section says nothing about anyone else
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether she is a female employee is not answered
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 76(1)(a)(i): "the period of 4 weeks immediately before her confinement".
-- src:2768 | (a) during —
-- src:2770 | (i) the period of 4 weeks immediately before her
-- src:2771 | confinement; and
-- src:2773 | (ii) the period of 8 weeks immediately after her
-- src:2774 | confinement;
@ref s 76(1)(a) (src:2768-2774)
GIVEN `the day of the confinement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Period of days`
`s 76(1)(a)(i) the 4 weeks immediately before the confinement` MEANS
    `Period of days` WITH
        `first day` IS `the day of the confinement` MINUS 28
        `last day` IS `the day of the confinement` MINUS 1

-- s 76(1)(a)(ii): "the period of 8 weeks immediately after her confinement".
@ref s 76(1)(a)(ii) (src:2768-2774)
GIVEN `the day of the confinement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Period of days`
`s 76(1)(a)(ii) the 8 weeks immediately after the confinement` MEANS
    `Period of days` WITH
        `first day` IS `the day of the confinement`
        `last day` IS `the day of the confinement` PLUS 55

-- s 76(1)(b): "a period of 12 weeks, as agreed to by her and her employer, commencing (i) not
-- earlier than 28 days immediately preceding the day of her confinement; and (ii) not later
-- than the day of her confinement".  Outside that window the paragraph does not give the period.
-- src:2776 | (b) during a period of 12 weeks, as agreed to by her and her
-- src:2777 | employer, commencing —
-- src:2782 | (i) not earlier than 28 days immediately preceding the
-- src:2783 | day of her confinement; and
-- src:2785 | (ii) not later than the day of her confinement; or
@ref s 76(1)(b) (src:2776-2785)
GIVEN `the day of the confinement` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the agreed period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Period of days`)
`s 76(1)(b) the agreed 12 weeks` MEANS
    IF `the first day of the agreed period` AT LEAST `the day of the confinement` MINUS 28
       AND `the first day of the agreed period` AT MOST `the day of the confinement`
    THEN JUST (`Period of days` WITH
            `first day` IS `the first day of the agreed period`
            `last day` IS `the first day of the agreed period` PLUS 83)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the 12 weeks must commence not earlier than 28 days before the day of the confinement and not later than that day; this type is a period and cannot say no, so the twin below does (fork F18, ruling (a) of 2026-11-05)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The twin of the rule above that can say no: the text fixes the window in its own words
-- ("not earlier than 28 days immediately preceding the day of her confinement" and "not later than
-- the day of her confinement"), so a start outside it is the text's no (Meng, 2026-11-05, ruling (a)).
-- src:2776 | (b) during a period of 12 weeks, as agreed to by her and her
-- src:2777 | employer, commencing —
-- src:2782 | (i) not earlier than 28 days immediately preceding the
-- src:2783 | day of her confinement; and
-- src:2785 | (ii) not later than the day of her confinement; or
@ref s 76(1)(b) (src:2776-2785)
GIVEN `the day of the confinement` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the agreed period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(1)(b) the agreed 12 weeks begin inside the window` MEANS
    IF `the first day of the agreed period` AT LEAST `the day of the confinement` MINUS 28
       AND `the first day of the agreed period` AT MOST `the day of the confinement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not earlier than 28 days immediately preceding the day of her confinement"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 76(1)(c)(i): "a period of 8 weeks, as agreed to by her and her employer, commencing (A) not
-- earlier than 28 days immediately preceding the day of her confinement; and (B) not later than
-- the day of her confinement".
-- src:2787 | (c) during —
-- src:2789 | (i) a period of 8 weeks, as agreed to by her and her
-- src:2790 | employer, commencing —
-- src:2792 | (A) not earlier than 28 days immediately preceding
-- src:2793 | the day of her confinement; and
-- src:2795 | (B) not later than the day of her confinement; and
@ref s 76(1)(c)(i) (src:2787-2795)
GIVEN `the day of the confinement` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the agreed period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Period of days`)
`s 76(1)(c)(i) the agreed 8 weeks` MEANS
    IF `the first day of the agreed period` AT LEAST `the day of the confinement` MINUS 28
       AND `the first day of the agreed period` AT MOST `the day of the confinement`
    THEN JUST (`Period of days` WITH
            `first day` IS `the first day of the agreed period`
            `last day` IS `the first day of the agreed period` PLUS 55)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the 8 weeks must commence not earlier than 28 days before the day of the confinement and not later than that day; this type is a period and cannot say no, so the twin below does (fork F18, ruling (a) of 2026-11-05)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The twin of the rule above that can say no (ruling (a) of 2026-11-05, as for s 76(1)(b)).
-- src:2787 | (c) during —
-- src:2789 | (i) a period of 8 weeks, as agreed to by her and her
-- src:2790 | employer, commencing —
-- src:2792 | (A) not earlier than 28 days immediately preceding
-- src:2793 | the day of her confinement; and
-- src:2795 | (B) not later than the day of her confinement; and
@ref s 76(1)(c)(i) (src:2787-2795)
GIVEN `the day of the confinement` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the agreed period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(1)(c)(i) the agreed 8 weeks begin inside the window` MEANS
    IF `the first day of the agreed period` AT LEAST `the day of the confinement` MINUS 28
       AND `the first day of the agreed period` AT MOST `the day of the confinement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not earlier than 28 days immediately preceding the day of her confinement"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 76(1)(c)(ii): further periods "in aggregate no shorter than as reckoned in accordance with
-- the Fifth Schedule or 24 days, whichever is the lower".  The Fifth Schedule is part ea3's;
-- its answer is an input (seam S8).  If it is not known, "the lower" of it and 24 is not known.
-- src:2797 | (ii) one or more than one period each of such duration as
-- src:2798 | agreed between the employee and her employer but
-- src:2799 | in aggregate no shorter than as reckoned in
-- src:2800 | accordance with the Fifth Schedule or 24 days,
-- src:2801 | whichever is the lower, all of which must be taken
-- src:2802 | within the period of 12 months commencing on the
-- src:2803 | day of her confinement.
@ref s 76(1)(c)(ii) (src:2797-2803)
GIVEN `the answer of sch 5 days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 76(1)(c)(ii) the least total of the further periods, in days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of sch 5 days`
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        IF d LESS THAN 24 THEN JUST d ELSE JUST 24
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the number of days reckoned under the Fifth Schedule is not given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 76(1)(c)(ii): "all of which must be taken within the period of 12 months commencing on the
-- day of her confinement".  The 12 months run from the day of the confinement (daydate `add months`
-- clamps the day to the end of a short month).
@ref s 76(1)(c)(ii) (src:2797-2803)
GIVEN `the day of the confinement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Period of days`
`s 76(1)(c)(ii) the 12 months within which the further periods must be taken` MEANS
    `Period of days` WITH
        `first day` IS `the day of the confinement`
        `last day` IS `add months` `the day of the confinement` 12 MINUS 1

-- A helper for the next rule: the number of days in a period, both ends counted.
GIVEN p IS A `Period of days`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 76(1)(c)(ii) helper: the days in the period` MEANS
    p's `last day` MINUS p's `first day` PLUS 1

-- A helper for the next rule: every period in the list begins and ends inside the window.
GIVEN window IS A `Period of days`
      periods IS A LIST OF `Period of days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 76(1)(c)(ii) helper: every period lies inside the window` MEANS
    CONSIDER periods
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        p's `first day` AT LEAST window's `first day`
        AND p's `last day` AT MOST window's `last day`
        AND `s 76(1)(c)(ii) helper: every period lies inside the window` window rest

-- s 76(1)(c)(ii) as a test of the periods actually taken: the further periods taken in
-- aggregate are no shorter than the least total, and all of them fall in the 12 months.
@ref s 76(1)(c)(ii) (src:2797-2803)
GIVEN `the answer of sch 5 days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the further periods taken` IS A LIST OF `Period of days`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(1)(c)(ii) helper: the total of the further periods is long enough` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 76(1)(c)(ii) the least total of the further periods, in days` `the answer of sch 5 days`
    WHEN JUST least THEN
        IF sum (map `s 76(1)(c)(ii) helper: the days in the period` `the further periods taken`) AT LEAST least
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in aggregate no shorter than as reckoned in"
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the least total depends on the Fifth Schedule, which is not given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@ref s 76(1)(c)(ii) (src:2797-2803)
GIVEN `the day of the confinement` IS A DATE
      `the answer of sch 5 days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the further periods taken` IS A LIST OF `Period of days`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(1)(c)(ii) the further periods taken satisfy the paragraph` MEANS
    IF `s 76(1)(c)(ii) helper: every period lies inside the window` (`s 76(1)(c)(ii) the 12 months within which the further periods must be taken` `the day of the confinement`) `the further periods taken`
    THEN `s 76(1)(c)(ii) helper: the total of the further periods is long enough` `the answer of sch 5 days` `the further periods taken`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "all of which must be taken within the period of 12 months commencing on the day of her confinement"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§ `Part 9 -- the benefit period and the payment for it (s 76(1A), (3))`

-- Which of the three patterns of s 76(1) the female employee takes.
DECLARE `s 76(1A) Pattern of absence` IS ONE OF
    `s 76(1A) absence under subsection (1)(a)`
    `s 76(1A) absence under subsection (1)(b)`
    `s 76(1A) absence under subsection (1)(c)`

-- s 76(1A): the benefit period is (a) the 4 weeks before and the first 4 weeks of the 8 weeks after;
-- (b) the first 8 weeks of the 12 weeks; (c) the 8 weeks of (1)(c)(i).  Under (a) the two pieces
-- meet at the day of the confinement (fork F1), so the benefit period is one stretch of 56 days.
-- Under (b) and (c) the agreed period must start in the window of those paragraphs; if it does not,
-- the paragraph gives no period and this answers NOTHING.
-- src:2807 | (1A) Subject to this section and section 77, every female employee
-- src:2808 | is entitled to receive payment from her employer at her gross rate of
-- src:2809 | pay for any of the following periods (called in this Part the benefit
-- src:2810 | period):
-- src:2812 | (a) where subsection (1)(a) applies, the period of 4 weeks
-- src:2813 | referred to in subsection (1)(a)(i) and the first 4 weeks of
-- src:2814 | the period referred to in subsection (1)(a)(ii);
-- src:2816 | (b) where subsection (1)(b) applies, the first 8 weeks of the
-- src:2817 | period referred to in subsection (1)(b);
-- src:2819 | (c) where subsection (1)(c) applies, the period of 8 weeks
-- src:2820 | referred to in subsection (1)(c)(i).
@ref s 76(1A) (src:2807-2820)
GIVEN pattern IS A `s 76(1A) Pattern of absence`
      `the day of the confinement` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the agreed period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Period of days`)
`s 76(1A) the benefit period` MEANS
    CONSIDER pattern
    WHEN `s 76(1A) absence under subsection (1)(a)` THEN
        JUST (`Period of days` WITH
            `first day` IS `the day of the confinement` MINUS 28
            `last day` IS `the day of the confinement` PLUS 27)
    WHEN `s 76(1A) absence under subsection (1)(b)` THEN
        CONSIDER `s 76(1)(b) the agreed 12 weeks` `the day of the confinement` `the first day of the agreed period`
        WHEN JUST p THEN
            JUST (`Period of days` WITH
                `first day` IS p's `first day`
                `last day` IS p's `first day` PLUS 55)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the 12 weeks of subsection (1)(b) must commence in the window that paragraph sets
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `s 76(1A) absence under subsection (1)(c)` THEN
        `s 76(1)(c)(i) the agreed 8 weeks` `the day of the confinement` `the first day of the agreed period`

-- s 76(1A): "every female employee is entitled to receive payment from her employer at her gross
-- rate of pay for any of the following periods".  Subject to the rest of s 76 and to s 77.
@ref s 76(1A) (src:2807-2810)
GIVEN `the person is a female employee` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(1A) the female employee is entitled to payment at her gross rate of pay for the benefit period` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person is a female employee`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is to "every female employee"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether she is a female employee is not answered
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 76(1A) with s 77(1): the sum is the days paid times the gross rate of pay for a day.  The gross
-- rate per day is the Third Schedule's answer (seam S6); if it is not given the sum is not given.
@ref s 76(1A) (src:2807-2810)
GIVEN `the days of the benefit period for which payment is due` IS A NUMBER
      `the answer of sch 3 gross rate of pay per day` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 76(1A) the sum payable for the days of the benefit period` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of sch 3 gross rate of pay per day`
    WHEN JUST rate THEN JUST (`the days of the benefit period for which payment is due` TIMES rate)
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the gross rate of pay for a day is worked out under the Third Schedule, which is not given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 76(3): a female employee who worked on a day of the benefit period before the confinement gets,
-- in addition to the gross rate of pay for that day, an amount equal to a day's pay at the gross rate,
-- "or to absent herself from work on another day at the end of the benefit period".
-- The section does not say who chooses (fork F2); this rule gives the amount and the next one the days.
-- src:2865 | (3) Where a female employee has worked in her employment for
-- src:2866 | any day during the benefit period before her confinement, she is
-- src:2867 | entitled to receive in addition to her gross rate of pay for that day an
-- src:2868 | amount that is equivalent to a day’s pay at the gross rate of pay or to
-- src:2869 | absent herself from work on another day at the end of the benefit
-- src:2870 | period.
@ref s 76(3) (src:2865-2870)
GIVEN `the days she worked during the benefit period before the confinement` IS A NUMBER
      `the answer of sch 3 gross rate of pay per day` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 76(3) the amount equivalent to a day's pay for the days worked` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of sch 3 gross rate of pay per day`
    WHEN JUST rate THEN JUST (`the days she worked during the benefit period before the confinement` TIMES rate)
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the gross rate of pay for a day is worked out under the Third Schedule, which is not given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@ref s 76(3) (src:2865-2870)
GIVEN `the days she worked during the benefit period before the confinement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 76(3) the days she may absent herself instead at the end of the benefit period` MEANS
    `the days she worked during the benefit period before the confinement`

§ `Part 9 -- when a female employee is not paid (s 76(2) to (6))`

-- s 76(2): a delivery before 1 May 2013 whose estimated delivery date (as certified by a medical
-- practitioner) is also before 1 May 2013.  Not entitled to any pay during the benefit period if she
-- served the employer for less than 90 days immediately preceding the day of the confinement.
-- The section only takes the entitlement away; where it does not apply it says nothing.
-- src:2824 | (2) A female employee who delivers a child before 1 May 2013,
-- src:2825 | and whose estimated delivery date for her confinement in respect of
-- src:2826 | that child (as certified by a medical practitioner) is before 1 May
-- src:2827 | 2013, is not entitled to any pay during the benefit period if she has
-- src:2832 | served her employer for less than 90 days immediately preceding the
-- src:2833 | day of her confinement.
@ref s 76(2) (src:2824-2833)
GIVEN `the day she delivered` IS A DATE
      `the estimated delivery date for the confinement as certified by a medical practitioner` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the days she served her employer immediately preceding the day of her confinement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(2) the female employee is entitled to pay during the benefit period` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the estimated delivery date for the confinement as certified by a medical practitioner`
    WHEN JUST estimated THEN
        IF `the day she delivered` LESS THAN (Date 1 5 2013) AND estimated LESS THAN (Date 1 5 2013)
        THEN
            IF `the days she served her employer immediately preceding the day of her confinement` LESS THAN 90
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not entitled to any pay during the benefit period"
            THEN JUST FALSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection only takes the entitlement away from a person who served less than 90 days
            ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection applies only to a delivery, and an estimated delivery date, before 1 May 2013
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection applies only where the certified estimated delivery date is before 1 May 2013, and it is not given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- A helper for s 76(2A): the 3-month test.  "less than 3 months" is read on completed months.
GIVEN `the completed months she served her employer immediately preceding the day of her confinement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(2A) helper: not entitled if served less than 3 months` MEANS
    IF `the completed months she served her employer immediately preceding the day of her confinement` LESS THAN 3
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not entitled to any pay during the benefit period"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection only takes the entitlement away from a person who served less than 3 months
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 76(2A): (a) a delivery on or after 1 May 2013 but before 22 August 2015; or (b) a delivery before
-- 1 May 2013 whose certified estimated delivery date is on or after 1 May 2013.  Not entitled to any
-- pay during the benefit period if she served less than 3 months immediately before the confinement.
-- src:2837 | (2A) A female employee who delivers a child —
-- src:2839 | (a) on or after 1 May 2013 but before 22 August 2015; or
-- src:2841 | (b) before 1 May 2013 but whose estimated delivery date for
-- src:2842 | her confinement in respect of that child (as certified by a
-- src:2843 | medical practitioner) is on or after 1 May 2013,
-- src:2845 | is not entitled to any pay during the benefit period if she has served
-- src:2846 | her employer for less than 3 months immediately preceding the day of
-- src:2847 | her confinement.
@ref s 76(2A) (src:2837-2847)
GIVEN `the day she delivered` IS A DATE
      `the estimated delivery date for the confinement as certified by a medical practitioner` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the completed months she served her employer immediately preceding the day of her confinement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(2A) the female employee is entitled to pay during the benefit period` MEANS
    IF `the day she delivered` AT LEAST (Date 1 5 2013) AND `the day she delivered` LESS THAN (Date 22 8 2015)
    THEN `s 76(2A) helper: not entitled if served less than 3 months` `the completed months she served her employer immediately preceding the day of her confinement`
    ELSE
        CONSIDER `the estimated delivery date for the confinement as certified by a medical practitioner`
        WHEN JUST estimated THEN
            IF `the day she delivered` LESS THAN (Date 1 5 2013) AND estimated AT LEAST (Date 1 5 2013)
            THEN `s 76(2A) helper: not entitled if served less than 3 months` `the completed months she served her employer immediately preceding the day of her confinement`
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection applies only to the two kinds of delivery in paragraphs (a) and (b)
            ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) needs the certified estimated delivery date, and it is not given
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- A helper for s 76(2B): the 3-month test, in the words of that subsection.
GIVEN `the completed months she served her employer preceding the day of her confinement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(2B) helper: not entitled if not served at least 3 months` MEANS
    IF `the completed months she served her employer preceding the day of her confinement` LESS THAN 3
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not entitled to any pay during the benefit period"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection only takes the entitlement away from a person who has not served at least 3 months
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 76(2B): (a) a delivery on or after 22 August 2015; or (b) a delivery before 22 August 2015 whose
-- certified estimated delivery date is on or after that date.  Not entitled to any pay during the
-- benefit period if she has not served at least 3 months preceding the day of the confinement.
-- src:2851 | (2B) A female employee who delivers a child —
-- src:2853 | (a) on or after 22 August 2015; or
-- src:2855 | (b) before 22 August 2015 but whose estimated delivery date
-- src:2856 | for her confinement in respect of that child (as certified by
-- src:2857 | a medical practitioner) is on or after that date,
-- src:2859 | is not entitled to any pay during the benefit period if she has not
-- src:2860 | served her employer for a period of at least 3 months preceding the
-- src:2861 | day of her confinement.
@ref s 76(2B) (src:2851-2861)
GIVEN `the day she delivered` IS A DATE
      `the estimated delivery date for the confinement as certified by a medical practitioner` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the completed months she served her employer preceding the day of her confinement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(2B) the female employee is entitled to pay during the benefit period` MEANS
    IF `the day she delivered` AT LEAST (Date 22 8 2015)
    THEN `s 76(2B) helper: not entitled if not served at least 3 months` `the completed months she served her employer preceding the day of her confinement`
    ELSE
        CONSIDER `the estimated delivery date for the confinement as certified by a medical practitioner`
        WHEN JUST estimated THEN
            IF estimated AT LEAST (Date 22 8 2015)
            THEN `s 76(2B) helper: not entitled if not served at least 3 months` `the completed months she served her employer preceding the day of her confinement`
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection applies only to a delivery on or after 22 August 2015, or one before it with a certified estimated delivery date on or after it
            ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) needs the certified estimated delivery date, and it is not given
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 76(5): "Subsection (4) does not apply to such class or classes of employees as the Minister may,
-- by notification in the Gazette, specify".  Whether she is in a class so specified is a fact asked.
-- src:2885 | (5) Subsection (4) does not apply to such class or classes of
-- src:2886 | employees as the Minister may, by notification in the Gazette,
-- src:2887 | specify.
@ref s 76(5) (src:2885-2887)
GIVEN `she belongs to a class of employees the Minister has specified by notification in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(5) subsection (4) applies to the female employee` MEANS
    IF `she belongs to a class of employees the Minister has specified by notification in the Gazette`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not apply"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection does not say that subsection (4) applies to anyone; it only takes a specified class out
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 76(4): "Subject to any collective agreement or award to the contrary, a female employee is not
-- entitled to any payment under subsection (1A) for any confinement if, at the time of the
-- confinement (a) she has 2 or more living children; and (b) those children were born during more
-- than one previous confinement."
-- src:2872 | (4) Subject to any collective agreement or award to the contrary, a
-- src:2873 | female employee is not entitled to any payment under
-- src:2874 | subsection (1A) for any confinement if, at the time of the
-- src:2875 | confinement —
-- src:2877 | (a) she has 2 or more living children; and
-- src:2879 | (b) those children were born during more than one previous
-- src:2880 | confinement.
@ref s 76(4) (src:2872-2880)
GIVEN `the living children she has at the time of the confinement` IS A NUMBER
      `the previous confinements during which those children were born` IS A NUMBER
      `a collective agreement or award provides to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she belongs to a class of employees the Minister has specified by notification in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(4) the female employee is entitled to payment under subsection (1A) for the confinement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is "Subject to any collective agreement or award to the contrary"
        IF `a collective agreement or award provides to the contrary` THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (5) takes a specified class out of subsection (4)
        IF `s 76(5) subsection (4) applies to the female employee` `she belongs to a class of employees the Minister has specified by notification in the Gazette` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not entitled to any payment under subsection (1A) for any confinement"
        IF `the living children she has at the time of the confinement` AT LEAST 2
           AND `the previous confinements during which those children were born` AT LEAST 2
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection takes the payment away only from a person with 2 or more living children born in more than one previous confinement
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 76(5A): resigning before she has used the whole of an absence under (1)(a), (b) or (c).
-- src:2889 | (5A) Where the employment of a female employee is terminated
-- src:2890 | because she resigns before she has exercised, wholly or partly, her
-- src:2891 | entitlement to absent herself from work during a period mentioned in
-- src:2892 | subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), she forfeits the following upon
-- src:2893 | termination of her employment:
-- src:2895 | (a) that entitlement (or the balance of that entitlement) to
-- src:2896 | absent herself from work;
-- src:2898 | (b) the entitlement under this section (if any) to receive
-- src:2899 | payment from her employer at her gross rate of pay in
-- src:2900 | respect of the forfeited period of absence from work under
-- src:2901 | paragraph (a).
@ref s 76(5A) (src:2889-2901)
GIVEN `how the employment ended` IS A `How the employment ended`
      `part of the entitlement to absent herself is still unused when the employment ends` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(5A)(a) the female employee keeps the entitlement to absent herself from work` MEANS
    IF `how the employment ended` EQUALS `Ending: the employee resigned`
       AND `part of the entitlement to absent herself is still unused when the employment ends`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "she forfeits the following upon termination of her employment"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection never says she keeps the entitlement, so the case outside its "Where" is answered by the twin `s 76(5A)(a) the female employee forfeits the entitlement to absent herself from work` below
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2889 | (5A) Where the employment of a female employee is terminated
-- src:2890 | because she resigns before she has exercised, wholly or partly, her
