§ `Part 9 -- the days that are paid, and when the payment is made (ss 77 and 78)`

-- s 77(1): "The payment referred to in section 76 must be paid for every day of the benefit period,
-- including holidays, but not any day during the benefit period on which the female employee takes
-- no-pay leave."  A holiday in the benefit period is paid like any other day.
-- src:2916 | 77.—(1) The payment referred to in section 76 must be paid for
-- src:2917 | every day of the benefit period, including holidays, but not any day
-- src:2918 | during the benefit period on which the female employee takes no‑pay
-- src:2919 | leave.
@ref s 77(1) (src:2916-2919)
GIVEN `the day is within the benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 2(1) "no-pay leave"` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77(1) the payment referred to in section 76 must be paid for the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the day is within the benefit period` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the payment must be paid for "every day of the benefit period" and the section says nothing of other days
            NOTHING
        IF `the answer of s 2(1) "no-pay leave"` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but not any day during the benefit period on which the female employee takes no-pay leave"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the answer of s 2(1) "no-pay leave"` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether she takes no-pay leave on the day is the answer of s 2(1) "no-pay leave", which the Act did not give on these facts
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 77(2): "Nothing in this section requires an employer to pay to a female employee an extra day's
-- salary for a holiday which falls within the benefit period."
-- src:2923 | (2) Nothing in this section requires an employer to pay to a female
-- src:2924 | employee an extra day’s salary for a holiday which falls within the
-- src:2925 | benefit period.
@ref s 77(2) (src:2923-2925)
GIVEN `the holiday falls within the benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77(2) section 77 requires the employer to pay an extra day's salary for the holiday` MEANS
    IF `the holiday falls within the benefit period`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section requires an employer to pay"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of a holiday which falls within the benefit period
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 78(1): a daily-rated female employee is paid in 2 instalments.
-- src:2929 | 78.—(1) In the case of a female employee who is a daily‑rated
-- src:2930 | employee, the payment referred to in section 76 must be paid in
-- src:2931 | 2 instalments, the first for the period up to and including the day of
-- src:2936 | confinement, to be paid within 7 days from the date of confinement,
-- src:2937 | and the second, for the period after confinement, to be paid within
-- src:2938 | 7 days from the end of that period.
@ref s 78(1) (src:2929-2938)
GIVEN `she is a daily-rated employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(1) the payment is made in 2 instalments` MEANS
    IF `she is a daily-rated employee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) speaks of a female employee who is a daily-rated employee; subsection (2) deals with any other
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 78(1): the first instalment is "for the period up to and including the day of confinement".
-- The number of days of the benefit period in that instalment, counting the day of the confinement.
@ref s 78(1) (src:2929-2938)
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
      `the day of the confinement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 78(1) the days of the benefit period in the first instalment` MEANS
    max 0 (`the day of the confinement` MINUS `the first day of the benefit period` PLUS 1)

-- s 78(1): the first instalment "to be paid within 7 days from the date of confinement".  The
-- Interpretation Act s 50 counts a period of days from an event (the day itself is left out; a
-- Sunday or public holiday at the end is carried to the next day).  Staged module, unchanged.
@ref s 78(1) (src:2929-2938)
GIVEN `the day of the confinement` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 78(1) the last day for paying the first instalment` MEANS
    `the last day of a period of days from the event` `the day of the confinement` 7 `the public holidays` FALSE

-- s 78(1): the second instalment is "within 7 days from the end of that period" (the benefit period).
@ref s 78(1) (src:2929-2938)
GIVEN `the last day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 78(1) the last day for paying the second instalment` MEANS
    `the last day of a period of days from the event` `the last day of the benefit period` 7 `the public holidays` FALSE

-- The twins of the two rules above that can say no: the text fixes both periods in its own words
-- ("within 7 days from the date of confinement", "within 7 days from the end of that period"), so a
-- payment after the last day is the text's no (ruling (a) of 2026-11-05; fork F18).
@ref s 78(1) (src:2929-2938)
GIVEN `the day the first instalment is paid` IS A DATE
      `the day of the confinement` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(1) the first instalment is paid within 7 days from the date of confinement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 78(1) the last day for paying the first instalment` `the day of the confinement` `the public holidays`
    WHEN JUST last THEN
        IF `the day the first instalment is paid` AT MOST last
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to be paid within 7 days from the date of confinement"
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Interpretation Act module did not give the last day
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@ref s 78(1) (src:2929-2938)
GIVEN `the day the second instalment is paid` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(1) the second instalment is paid within 7 days from the end of the benefit period` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 78(1) the last day for paying the second instalment` `the last day of the benefit period` `the public holidays`
    WHEN JUST last THEN
        IF `the day the second instalment is paid` AT MOST last
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 7 days from the end of that period"
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Interpretation Act module did not give the last day
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 78(2): "In the case of any other female employee, the payment must be paid at such time as the
-- salary earned by the employee under her contract of service is due to be paid to her."
-- src:2940 | (2) In the case of any other female employee, the payment must be
-- src:2941 | paid at such time as the salary earned by the employee under her
-- src:2942 | contract of service is due to be paid to her.
@ref s 78(2) (src:2940-2942)
GIVEN `she is a daily-rated employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the salary she has earned is due to be paid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 78(2) the date by which the payment must be paid` MEANS
    IF `she is a daily-rated employee`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) speaks of "any other female employee"; a daily-rated employee is paid under subsection (1)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST `the date the salary she has earned is due to be paid`

§ `Part 9 -- if the female employee dies (s 79)`

-- Who is paid after her death: "to the person nominated by her under section 80(4) or, if there is
-- no such person, to her personal representative".
DECLARE `s 79 Person who is paid after her death` IS ONE OF
    `s 79 the person she nominated under section 80(4)`
    `s 79 her personal representative`

-- src:2947 | 79.—(1) If a female employee, after giving notice to her employer
-- src:2948 | under section 80(1), abstains from work in expectation of her
-- src:2949 | confinement and dies from any cause before her confinement, the
-- src:2950 | employer must pay to the person nominated by her under
-- src:2951 | section 80(4) or, if there is no such person, to her personal
-- src:2952 | representative a sum of money at the rate prescribed under
-- src:2953 | section 76 from the date immediately following the last day on
-- src:2954 | which she worked to the day immediately preceding the day of her
-- src:2955 | death and except in the circumstances mentioned in this subsection no
-- src:2956 | employer is liable to pay any sum in respect of a period exceeding
-- src:2957 | 30 days.
@ref s 79(1) (src:2947-2957)
GIVEN `she nominated a person under section 80(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 79 Person who is paid after her death`
`s 79(1) the person to whom the employer must pay` MEANS
    IF `she nominated a person under section 80(4)`
    THEN `s 79 the person she nominated under section 80(4)`
    ELSE `s 79 her personal representative`

-- s 79(1): "If a female employee, after giving notice to her employer under section 80(1), abstains from
-- work in expectation of her confinement and dies from any cause before her confinement, the employer
-- must pay ...".
@ref s 79(1) (src:2947-2957)
GIVEN `she gave notice to her employer under section 80(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she abstained from work in expectation of her confinement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she died before her confinement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(1) the employer must pay a sum of money after her death` MEANS
    IF `she gave notice to her employer under section 80(1)`
       AND `she abstained from work in expectation of her confinement`
       AND `she died before her confinement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a female employee, after giving notice to her employer under section 80(1)"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 79(1): the sum runs "from the date immediately following the last day on which she worked to the
-- day immediately preceding the day of her death", both ends counted.
@ref s 79(1) (src:2947-2957)
GIVEN `the last day on which she worked` IS A DATE
      `the day of her death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 79(1) the days for which the sum is payable` MEANS
    max 0 (`the day of her death` MINUS `the last day on which she worked` MINUS 1)

-- s 79(1): "a sum of money at the rate prescribed under section 76".  Section 76 prescribes one rate,
-- the gross rate of pay (s 76(1A)); fork F3.  The gross rate for a day is the Third Schedule's answer (seam S6).
@ref s 79(1) (src:2947-2957)
GIVEN `the days for which the sum is payable` IS A NUMBER
      `the answer of sch 3 gross rate of pay per day` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 79(1) the sum payable` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of sch 3 gross rate of pay per day`
    WHEN JUST rate THEN JUST (`the days for which the sum is payable` TIMES rate)
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the gross rate of pay for a day is worked out under the Third Schedule, which is not given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 79(1): "except in the circumstances mentioned in this subsection no employer is liable to pay any
-- sum in respect of a period exceeding 30 days".  Read here as it stands, for a period outside the
-- circumstances of the subsection (fork F4: the Act does not say which "period" it caps).
@ref s 79(1) (src:2947-2957)
GIVEN `the circumstances mentioned in section 79(1) exist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(1) the employer is liable to pay a sum in respect of the period` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the circumstances mentioned in section 79(1) exist`) AND `the period in days` GREATER THAN 30
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no employer is liable to pay any sum in respect of a period exceeding 30 days"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the subsection does not say which period, other than the period of its own circumstances, it caps
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 79(2): "If a female employee dies from any cause on or after the day of her confinement and before
-- any payment to which she is entitled has been paid to her, the employer must pay ...".
-- src:2959 | (2) If a female employee dies from any cause on or after the day of
-- src:2960 | her confinement and before any payment to which she is entitled has
-- src:2961 | been paid to her, the employer must pay to the person nominated by
-- src:2962 | her under section 80(4) or, if there is no such person, to her personal
-- src:2963 | representative any sum of money to which she was on the date of her
-- src:2964 | death entitled in respect of the period up to the day of confinement
-- src:2965 | and in respect of the period after confinement up to the day
-- src:2966 | immediately preceding the day of her death.
@ref s 79(2) (src:2959-2966)
GIVEN `she died on or after the day of her confinement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a payment to which she was entitled had not been paid to her` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(2) the employer must pay a sum of money after her death` MEANS
    IF `she died on or after the day of her confinement` AND `a payment to which she was entitled had not been paid to her`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a female employee dies from any cause on or after the day of her confinement"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 79(2): the sum is what she was entitled to "in respect of the period up to the day of confinement
-- and in respect of the period after confinement up to the day immediately preceding the day of her
-- death".  The days of the benefit period up to the day before her death, both ends counted.
@ref s 79(2) (src:2959-2966)
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
      `the day of her death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 79(2) the days of the benefit period up to the day before her death` MEANS
    max 0 (`the last day counted` MINUS `the first day of the benefit period` PLUS 1)
    WHERE
        `the last day counted` MEANS
            IF `the last day of the benefit period` LESS THAN `the day of her death` MINUS 1
            THEN `the last day of the benefit period`
            ELSE `the day of her death` MINUS 1

§ `Part 9 -- the notice a female employee gives, and the nominee (s 80)`

-- s 80(1): "A female employee must, at least one week before absenting herself from work in accordance
-- with section 76, give notice to her employer specifying the date on which she intends to commence
-- absenting herself from work."  The duty falls on a female employee who is to absent herself.
-- src:2970 | 80.—(1) A female employee must, at least one week before
-- src:2971 | absenting herself from work in accordance with section 76, give
-- src:2972 | notice to her employer specifying the date on which she intends to
-- src:2973 | commence absenting herself from work.
@ref s 80(1) (src:2970-2973)
GIVEN `the person is a female employee` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 80(1) the female employee must give her employer notice of the date she intends to begin absenting herself` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person is a female employee`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is a duty of "A female employee"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether she is a female employee is not answered
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 80(1) as a count of days: "at least one week before" read as at least 7 days between the day the
-- notice is given and the first day she absents herself (fork F5: the Act does not say whether the two
-- days themselves are counted).  A plain comparison of two dates; it carries no legal conclusion.
@ref s 80(1) (src:2970-2973)
GIVEN `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE
      `the first day she absents herself from work` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 80(1) the notice is given at least one week before the first day of absence` MEANS
    `the first day she absents herself from work` MINUS `the day the notice is given` AT LEAST 7

-- s 80(2): "A female employee who has been confined must, as soon as practicable, inform her employer of
-- the date on which she was confined."
-- src:2978 | (2) A female employee who has been confined must, as soon as
-- src:2979 | practicable, inform her employer of the date on which she was
-- src:2980 | confined.
@ref s 80(2) (src:2978-2980)
GIVEN `the answer of s 2(1) "confinement"` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 80(2) the female employee who has been confined must inform her employer of the date of the confinement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of s 2(1) "confinement"`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is a duty of a female employee "who has been confined"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the event was a confinement is the answer of s 2(1) "confinement", which the Act did not give on these facts
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 80(3): omitting the notice of (1), or failing to inform under (2), costs half the payment "unless
-- she was prevented by any sufficient cause from giving the notice".
-- src:2982 | (3) Any female employee who omits to give notice as required
-- src:2983 | under subsection (1) or fails to inform her employer as required under
-- src:2984 | subsection (2) is entitled to only half the amount of any payment to
-- src:2985 | which she is entitled to under this Part unless she was prevented by
-- src:2986 | any sufficient cause from giving the notice.
@ref s 80(3) (src:2982-2986)
GIVEN `she omitted to give notice as required under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she failed to inform her employer as required under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she was prevented by a sufficient cause from giving the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 80(3) the female employee is entitled to only half the amount of the payment` MEANS
    IF `she omitted to give notice as required under subsection (1)` OR `she failed to inform her employer as required under subsection (2)`
    THEN
        IF `she was prevented by a sufficient cause from giving the notice`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless she was prevented by any sufficient cause from giving the notice"
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection applies only to a female employee who omits the notice of (1) or fails to inform under (2)
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 80(3) (src:2982-2986)
GIVEN `the payment to which she is entitled under this Part` IS A NUMBER
      `the answer of s 80(3) she is entitled to only half` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 80(3) the amount of the payment` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 80(3) she is entitled to only half` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`the payment to which she is entitled under this Part` DIVIDED BY 2)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection fixes the amount only when it limits her to half
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 80(4): "A female employee may at any time in writing nominate some other person to whom any payment ...
-- may be paid on her behalf; and any such payment made to the person so nominated is deemed ... to be
-- payment to the female employee who nominated the person."
-- src:2988 | (4) A female employee may at any time in writing nominate some
-- src:2989 | other person to whom any payment to which she is entitled under this
-- src:2990 | Part may be paid on her behalf; and any such payment made to the
-- src:2991 | person so nominated is deemed, for the purpose of this Act, to be
-- src:2992 | payment to the female employee who nominated the person.
@ref s 80(4) (src:2988-2992)
GIVEN `the nomination was made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment was made to the person nominated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 80(4) the payment is deemed to be payment to the female employee` MEANS
    IF `the nomination was made in writing` AND `the payment was made to the person nominated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is of a payment "made to the person so nominated", and the nomination must be "in writing"
    ELSE NOTHING
